00:25:52.000 --> 00:26:36.000
It wasn't in her nature to hurt anyone, especially not the very children she had been employed to look after. At one point, she even helped the kids set up a mini stand on the street to sell sweets and biscuits. But in the weeks leading up to Sophie's death, neighbors had seen less and less of her. During one visit to the local fish and chip shop, owner Michael could tell by Sophie's body language that something wasn't right. He'd suspected the nanny wasn't doing well, as he noticed she often had tears in her eyes. Michael asked Sophie what was wrong, and she confided that Sabrina had beat her.

