he let himself believe in her twisted reality and by doing so enabled and emboldened her. Another example of the folly adieu phenomenon is the Ericsson twins, covered in episode 17 of Case File. As for why Sophie didn't leave or otherwise seek help, it's likely that she didn't feel able to. Sabrina and Wiesem intimidated and bullied her to the point that she felt completely powerless, physically, mentally, and financially. Police never found her passport or the money her mother had given her for a return ticket to France. It's suspected the couple took them away to prevent Sophie from escaping. While Sophie's exact reasonings for staying would never be known, investigators did find a short note that she had written shortly before her murder.

